    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-057: `parent_content_height` threading + `%` height/max-height**. **Documentation only.** Implementation (~200 lines, 8 call sites) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\nCloses ADR-039's and ADR-053's explicit `%` deferrals. Unblocks ADR-058's `translateY` chain (the magnifier centering).\n\n## What's blocked today\n\n| Deferral | Since | Site |\n|---|---|---|\n| `height: %` skipped | ADR-039 | layout.cpp:1835 |\n| `min-height: %` skipped | ADR-039 | layout.cpp:1848 |\n| `max-height: %` skipped | ADR-039 / 053 | layout.cpp:1857 |\n| `top: 50%` doesn't resolve | ADR-054 | needs parent height |\n| `translateY(-50%)` centering | ADR-054 | needs parent height |\n\n`LengthContext` has `parent_content_width` (ADR-011) but not `parent_content_height`.\n\n## The threading shape\n\n`parent_content_width` is the model — clean 8-site mirror:\n\n| Where | Width | Height (new) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `LengthContext` field | ✅ line 23 | ADDED |\n| `layout_element` param | ✅ position 6, line 291 | ADDED |\n| `ctx.*` setter | ✅ line 372 | ADDED |\n| Recursive call sites | ✅ 8 sites | MIRRORED |\n\n## The circularity constraint (honest)\n\n`layout_element` recurses into children first, then applies its own `height:`. So a parent with `height: auto` **doesn't know its own content height during child layout.**\n\n**CSS spec resolves this:** child `height: %` on auto parent → treated as `auto` (skip). **This is correct behavior, not a limitation.** Chromium, Firefox, WebKit all do this.\n\n**Consequence:** the visible delta is narrower than the deferral list suggests. `%` heights on auto-height parents still skip. Only `%` on **fixed-height** parents resolve.\n\n## The `<html>` / `<body>` special case\n\n`<html>`'s containing block is viewport, not a parent element. CSS spec: `html { height: 100% }` resolves against viewport. ADR-052 made `viewport_h` correct in production.\n\n**So `<html>` / `<body>` resolve `%` against `viewport_h`, not `parent_content_height`.** Without this special case, `html, body { height: 100% }` — the near-universal CSS reset — would still skip, defeating the whole cycle for the most common case.\n\n## What ships (Shape B)\n\n- `LengthContext::parent_content_height`\n- `parse_length_for_height()` — `%` resolves against parent height\n- `layout_element` param + 8 call sites + `own_declared_content_height()` helper\n- 3 skip guards removed (`height`, `min-height`, `max-height`)\n- `<html>` / `<body>` special case\n- Test flip (test_box_model.cpp:109) + ~7 new tests\n- Fixture `docs/adr057-percent-height-test.html`\n\n## Visible delta\n\n**`html, body { height: 100% }` now resolves** — the CSS reset used by nearly every site starts working. On short pages, the body background covers the full viewport (visible but correct).\n\n**`height: N%` on fixed-height parents** resolves correctly.\n\n**`min-height` / `max-height` with `%`** on fixed-height parents resolve.\n\n## What this PR does NOT do\n\n- **Magnifier still ~10px high.** `top: 50%` + `translateY(-50%)` deferred to ADR-058. Shipping `top: 50%` alone moves the magnifier from y=7 to y=28 (worse). ADR-057 is the prerequisite; ADR-058 is the fix.\n- **Auto-height parents still skip `%`** — CSS spec.\n- **`%` width, `%` margin, `%` padding** — untouched (already work against `parent_content_width`).\n\n## Regression risks flagged in the spec\n\n- **`html, body { height: 100% }` resolving** changes every page's body height from \"content height\" to \"viewport height.\" On short pages (docs/demo.html), body background paints across the full viewport. **Visible but correct.**\n- **Existing test at test_box_model.cpp:109** flips (asserts current skip)\n- **Explicit `height: Npx` on parents** now makes children's `%` heights resolve — some tests may reveal this\n\n## The magnifier chain (after ADR-057)\n\n| Layer | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `background-image` renders | ✅ ADR-056 |\n| `parent_content_height` available | ✅ **ADR-057 (this PR)** |\n| `top: 50%` resolves | ⏸ ADR-058 |\n| `translateY(-50%)` centers | ⏸ ADR-058 |\n\nOne step closer, one step to go.\n\n## Test count target\n\n- 663 → ~670 (+7 tests, 1 flipped)\n\nRefs #251\n",
